  "body": "## What changed\n- The tool page side preview draws the bands from the new `tool_body::checked_bands`. It uses `tool_body::checked_profile` (the machine-default floor that `judged` now also calls) and then `tool_body::stack`. This is the stack that the collision check sweeps. The UI has no second derivation. The collision shape is not changed.\n- The 3D mesh view shows only while a Pick button is armed. At rest the page has one preview.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2017-one-tool-preview.md`. The 3D view is the only surface where a click picks the tip or axis. Full removal would remove that function.\n\n## Tests\n- `the_tool_page_shows_one_preview_and_no_idle_3d_view`: one side view and no 3D view at rest. An armed pick shows the 3D view.\n- `the_side_preview_bands_are_the_collision_stack_of_an_explicit_body`: preview bands equal `stack(judged profile)`.\n- `without_a_body_the_side_preview_has_no_envelope_bands` and `tool_preview_without_body_draws_the_collision_cylinder`: with no body the drawn holder has the proportions of `HolderStack::cylinder`.\n- `the_preview_zoom_clamps_and_fit_resets_it` now arms Pick first.\n- Quick gate: post suites ok, app suites ok, `mcp_post_options` ok, ui suites ok (rerun after the zoom test fix). Clippy `-D warnings` on `camcraft-ui` and `camcraft-app` is clean.\n\n## Screenshots\nThe same applied holder fixture is rendered through the kittest app shell in both images.\nBefore restores the previous idle 3D view. After shows the single side preview at rest.\nImages are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\nBefore:\n![Before: side and 3D previews at rest](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/cede9911cb0e776e9020a77753d053f7b719057f/2096/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n![After: one side preview at rest](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/cede9911cb0e776e9020a77753d053f7b719057f/2096/after.png)\n\n## Not exercised\n- The real app window (the PNGs come from the kittest renderer).\n- The lathe Body tab was changed by one call (`placement_view`) and was not opened by hand.\n- Overlap: open PR #2081 changes only ribbon and theme code and the module list of `tests.rs`. A one-line textual conflict in `tests.rs` is possible.\n\nChangelog: The tool page shows one side preview that draws the holder shape the collision check reads. The 3D body view shows only while a Pick button is armed.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2017\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
